From: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH BlueZ] a2dp: Check setup->stream before setting the transport

transport_cb() runs from bt_io_accept() and begins by confirming that the
a2dp_setup it was handed still exists:

	if (!g_slist_find(setups, setup)) {
		warn("bt_io_accept: setup %p no longer valid", setup);
		...
	}

That establishes the lifetime of the setup, not of the stream it points at.
Several paths in a2dp.c clear setup->stream while leaving the setup itself on
the list, so by the time the accept completes the setup can be valid and its
stream NULL. It is then passed on unchecked:

	if (!avdtp_stream_set_transport(setup->stream,
					g_io_channel_unix_get_fd(io),
					imtu, omtu))

and avdtp_stream_set_transport() dereferences it immediately:

	gboolean avdtp_stream_set_transport(struct avdtp_stream *stream, ...)
	{
		GIOChannel *io = g_io_channel_unix_new(fd);

		if (stream != stream->session->pending_open) {

Observed on a QCA9377 (13d3:3503) whose controller stops answering HCI during
audio use. From the retained core, %r13 held NULL and the faulting instruction
was the first field load off it:

  bluetoothd[398112]: segfault at 10 ip 0000635d944b47e5 sp 00007ffefcba28d0 \
      error 4 in bluetoothd[367e5,635d944a3000+f3000]

  r13  0x0
  => 0x635d944b47e5:  mov 0x10(%r13),%rdi

Check the stream immediately before it is used, so every existing path keeps
its current behaviour up to the point that was previously unsafe. In
particular an bt_io_accept() error or a bt_io_get() failure still reports the
real I/O error rather than this secondary lifecycle condition.

125a2e237e7c ("a2dp: Fix possible crash when accepting stream transport")
previously hardened this same asynchronous accept window against the whole
setup disappearing while the accept was pending. This covers the remaining
case where the setup survives and its stream does not.

Signed-off-by: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
---
 profiles/audio/a2dp.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/profiles/audio/a2dp.c b/profiles/audio/a2dp.c
--- a/profiles/audio/a2dp.c
+++ b/profiles/audio/a2dp.c
@@ -2672,6 +2672,11 @@
 		goto drop;
 	}

+	if (!setup->stream) {
+		error("bt_io_accept: setup %p has no stream", setup);
+		goto drop;
+	}
+
 	if (!avdtp_stream_set_transport(setup->stream,
 					g_io_channel_unix_get_fd(io),
 					imtu, omtu))
--
